---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const code = `<iframe src="${SITE_URL}/embed/en/next-holiday/" title="Countdown to the next public holiday in your state" width="100%" height="560" style="border:0;max-width:1100px" loading="lazy"></iframe>`;
---
<PageLayout title="Embed the countdown to the next public holiday, by state" description="Show the countdown to the next public holiday in each Australian state on your club, school or council website for free: copy the code once and later holidays appear on their own." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Widget', path: route('widget', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Widget' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <header class="mb-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Embed the public holiday countdown</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-navy-700">For sports clubs, schools, councils and local media: visitors pick their state and see whether today is a public holiday, how long until the next one and the school term.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Code to copy</h2>
    <pre class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-navy-900 p-4 text-sm text-white"><code>{code}</code></pre>
    <p>The countdown runs on the lists published so far; when a state publishes a new year, we add it after checking, and the embedded countdown shows it without any change on your side. Terms: the credit line under the countdown stays visible, the countdown is not altered and comes without warranty. What visitors choose stays on their device. Questions via <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-navy-200">
    <iframe src={`/embed/${lang}/next-holiday/`} title="Countdown to the next public holiday in your state" width="100%" height="560" style="border:0" loading="lazy"></iframe>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
